   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Futur I",
     "texto": [
      "It is formed with conjugated **werden** and the infinitive at the end: **In zwei Jahren werde ich mein Studium abschließen** (in two years I'll finish my studies). It is used for plans, promises and predictions. In everyday speech the present with a time word is used more: **Nächstes Jahr fahre ich nach Italien** (next year I'm going to Italy)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Assumption with wohl",
     "texto": [
      "To say something probable, use **werden** + **wohl** + infinitive: **Er wird wohl krank sein** (he's probably ill). With the idea of \"probably\", **wohl** or **vermutlich** is used.",
      "Watch out for the false friend: **wohl** doesn't mean \"well\"; it means \"probably\"."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
